++/* The used-libs mask decides which luaopen_* the link keeps. A library the
++   mask omits is genuinely ABSENT from the exe: _G.os is nil and
++   package.loaded.os is nil, silently, with exit 0. So the mask is only correct
++   when the program provably cannot REACH the library.
++   A standard library table is reachable only through a container that holds
++   it, and in a closed world there are exactly three ways to obtain one:
++     (1) a constant-key global read -- `os.clock`, `_G.os` -- which is what the
++         constant scan below models, and which names the library;
++     (2) the globals table itself as a value (`_G[k]`, `pairs(_ENV)`,
++         `setmetatable({}, {__index = _G})`) -- lc_module_reflects_globals;
++     (3) the LOADED table, reachable as `package.loaded` (lc_module_reflects_package)
