++   `require` of a computed name is already a compile error (closed world), and
++   `load`/`loadstring`/`dofile`/`string.dump` do not exist, so there is no
++   fourth route. When (2) or (3) holds the compiler cannot see which library a
++   run-time key will ask for, and the ONLY sound answer is to link them all.
++   Set CLUA_LIBS_DEBUG=1 to see the mask and the reason on stderr. */
  unsigned lc_module_used_libs(LcModule *m) {
    unsigned mask = 0;
    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < m->nfuncs; i++) {
@@@ -91,6 -91,6 +134,17 @@@
